LESSONS={{"Algebra","Linear equations","Keep both sides equal. Distribute, collect like terms, then isolate the variable.","3(2x-1)=15|Expand: 6x-3=15.|Add 3: 6x=18.|Divide by 6: x=3.|Check: 3(6-1)=15.","Solve 5x-7=18.","x=5; add 7, then divide by 5."},{"Algebra","Inequalities","Reverse the inequality when multiplying or dividing by a negative number. Test boundary points separately.","-2x+3>11|Subtract 3: -2x>8.|Divide by -2 and reverse: x<-4.|Interval: (-infinity,-4).","Solve -3x<=12.","x>=-4; the endpoint is included."},{"Algebra","Absolute value","|u| is distance from zero. For c>=0, |u|=c gives u=c or u=-c. A negative right side has no solution.","|2x-3|=7|Branch 1: 2x-3=7 gives x=5.|Branch 2: 2x-3=-7 gives x=-2.|Both pass substitution.","Solve |x+1|=4.","x=3 or x=-5."},{"Algebra","Powers and radicals","For positive bases: x^a*x^b=x^(a+b); (x^a)^b=x^(ab). Even roots require nonnegative real radicands. sqrt(x^2)=|x|.","sqrt(72)|Factor: 72=36*2.|Take the square root of 36.|Answer: 6*sqrt(2).","Simplify sqrt(50).","5*sqrt(2)."},{"Functions","Domain and range","Domain lists allowed inputs. Exclude zero denominators, negative even-root inputs, and nonpositive logarithm inputs. Range lists outputs.","f(x)=sqrt(x-2)/(x-5)|Require x-2>=0, so x>=2.|Also require x!=5.|Domain: [2,5) union (5,infinity).","Find domain of ln(4-x).","x<4, since 4-x>0."},{"Functions","Composition","(f o g)(x)=f(g(x)). Apply the inner function first; enforce both domain restrictions.","f(x)=x^2+1, g(x)=3x|Replace x in f by 3x.|f(g(x))=(3x)^2+1=9x^2+1.|At x=2, the output is 37.","f(x)=2x+1, g(x)=x-4. Find f(g(3)).","-1: g(3)=-1, then f(-1)=-1."},{"Functions","Inverse functions","A function has an inverse function on a domain where it is one-to-one. Swap x and y, solve for y, and swap domain/range.","y=3x-5|Swap: x=3y-5.|Add 5 and divide by 3.|f^(-1)(x)=(x+5)/3.","Inverse of f(x)=2x+6?","(x-6)/2."},{"Functions","Transformations","For y=a*f(b*(x-h))+k: shift right h, up k; vertical scale |a|; horizontal scale 1/|b|. Negative a or b reflects.","y=-2(x-3)^2+4|Start with y=x^2.|Shift right 3; stretch vertically by 2.|Reflect across x-axis; move up 4.|Vertex (3,4); range y<=4.","Vertex of (x+2)^2-7?","(-2,-7)."},{"Functions","Average rate of change","Average rate on [a,b] is (f(b)-f(a))/(b-a), with a!=b. This is the slope of the secant line.","f(x)=x^2 on [1,4]|f(4)=16; f(1)=1.|Change in output: 15.|Change in input: 3.|Average rate: 5.","Average rate of x^2 on [2,5]?","7."},{"Polynomials","Quadratic equations","For ax^2+bx+c=0 with a!=0, D=b^2-4ac and x=(-b +/- sqrt(D))/(2a). D<0 gives complex roots.","x^2-5x+6=0|Factor: (x-2)(x-3)=0.|Zero product rule gives x=2 or 3.|Check both in the original.","Solve x^2-9=0.","x=3 or x=-3."},{"Polynomials","Vertex form","Complete the square or use h=-b/(2a), k=f(h). Then f(x)=a(x-h)^2+k.","x^2+6x+5|x^2+6x=(x+3)^2-9.|So f(x)=(x+3)^2-4.|Vertex (-3,-4); minimum -4.","Vertex of x^2-4x+1?","(2,-3)."},{"Polynomials","Division and zeros","If P(r)=0, then x-r is a factor. Synthetic division works for a monic linear divisor x-r. Include zero coefficients.","Divide x^3-6x^2+11x-6 by x-1.|Use r=1 and coefficients 1,-6,11,-6.|Bring down 1; multiply/add: -5,6,0.|Quotient x^2-5x+6; remainder 0.|All roots: 1,2,3.","Remainder of x^2+2x+3 divided by x-2?","P(2)=11."},{"Polynomials","End behavior and roots","Leading degree and coefficient control end behavior. Even multiplicity usually touches the axis; odd multiplicity crosses.","P(x)=-2(x-1)^2(x+3)|Degree 3, leading coefficient -2.|Left end up; right end down.|Root 1 has multiplicity 2: touches.|Root -3 has multiplicity 1: crosses.","Ends of a positive-leading quartic?","Both ends rise."},{"Rational","Rational functions","Factor first. Cancel common factors but keep original exclusions. Canceled factors create holes; remaining denominator zeros give vertical asymptotes.","(x^2-1)/(x-1)|Factor numerator: (x-1)(x+1).|For x!=1, simplify to x+1.|Hole at (1,2), not a vertical asymptote.","Simplify (x^2-4)/(x-2).","x+2 for x!=2; hole at (2,4)."},{"Rational","Asymptotes","After cancellation, compare numerator and denominator degrees. Lower numerator: y=0. Equal degrees: ratio of leading coefficients. One higher: divide for slant line.","(2x^2+1)/(x^2-4)|Equal degrees: horizontal asymptote y=2.|Denominator zeros at +/-2 do not cancel.|Vertical asymptotes x=-2 and x=2.","Horizontal asymptote of 3x/(x^2+1)?","y=0."},{"Rational","Rational inequalities","Move everything to one side, factor, mark zeros and excluded points, then test each interval. Never multiply by an unknown-sign denominator without cases.","(x-1)/(x+2)>0|Critical points: -2 (excluded), 1 (zero).|Signs on three intervals: +, -, +.|Answer: (-infinity,-2) union (1,infinity).","Where is (x-2)/(x+1)<0?","(-1,2)."},{"Exponents & logs","Logarithm rules","log_b(x)=y means b^y=x; b>0, b!=1, x>0. Products become sums; quotients become differences; powers become multipliers.","log_2(32)|Ask: 2 raised to what power is 32?|2^5=32.|Answer: 5.","Evaluate log_3(1/9).","-2."},{"Exponents & logs","Exponential equations","Isolate the exponential. Match bases when possible; otherwise take logarithms. Check the isolated quantity is positive.","3*2^x=21|Divide by 3: 2^x=7.|Take ln: x*ln(2)=ln(7).|x=ln(7)/ln(2), about 2.80735.","Solve 5^(x-1)=25.","x=3."},{"Exponents & logs","Log equations","Record positive-argument restrictions before combining logs. Solve the resulting equation, then reject candidates outside the domain.","ln(x)+ln(x-3)=ln(4)|Domain: x>3.|ln(x(x-3))=ln(4).|x^2-3x-4=0 gives 4 or -1.|Only x=4 is allowed.","Solve log_10(x-2)=2.","x=102; x>2."},{"Exponents & logs","Growth and decay","Discrete growth: A=P*(1+r)^t. Continuous growth: A=P*exp(k*t). Use negative rates for decay and keep time units consistent.","100 grows 5% per year for 3 years.|A=100*(1.05)^3.|A=115.7625, about 115.76.|This is compound, not simple growth.","Half-life 4 years: fraction after 12 years?","(1/2)^3=1/8."},{"Trigonometry","Radians and unit circle","180 degrees=pi radians. On the unit circle, (x,y)=(cos(t),sin(t)); tan(t)=sin(t)/cos(t) when cos(t)!=0.","t=150 degrees=5pi/6|Reference angle 30 degrees.|Quadrant II: sine +, cosine -.|sin(t)=1/2; cos(t)=-sqrt(3)/2.|tan(t)=-1/sqrt(3).","sin(pi/6)?","1/2."},{"Trigonometry","Right triangles","SOH-CAH-TOA: sin=opposite/hypotenuse, cos=adjacent/hypotenuse, tan=opposite/adjacent. Match degree/radian mode to the question.","Legs 3 and 4; hypotenuse 5.|Angle opposite the 3-unit side:|sin(t)=3/5.|t=asin(3/5), about 36.8699 degrees.","Opposite=5, hypotenuse=13. Find sine.","5/13."},{"Trigonometry","Trig graphs","For A*sin(B*(x-h))+D: amplitude |A|, period 2pi/|B| (radians), shift h, midline D. Tangent has period pi/|B|.","y=3*sin(2x)-1|Amplitude 3; midline -1.|Period pi radians.|Range [-4,2].","Period of cos(4x), in radians?","pi/2."},{"Trigonometry","Identities","sin^2(t)+cos^2(t)=1. Also 1+tan^2(t)=sec^2(t). Simplify one side at a time and retain all denominator restrictions.","(1-cos^2(t))/sin(t)|Replace numerator with sin^2(t).|Cancel one sine factor.|Equals sin(t), only where sin(t)!=0.","Simplify sin(t)/cos(t).","tan(t), where cos(t)!=0."},{"Trigonometry","Trig equations","Find a reference angle, select quadrants, then add all full periods. If the angle contains a factor, divide the entire solution by it.","sin(x)=1/2 in [0,2pi)|Reference angle pi/6.|Sine positive in I and II.|x=pi/6 or 5pi/6.|General: add 2pi*k to each, integer k.","cos(x)=0 in [0,2pi)?","pi/2 and 3pi/2."},{"Trigonometry","Sum and double angles","sin(u+v)=sin(u)cos(v)+cos(u)sin(v). cos(2u)=1-2sin^2(u)=2cos^2(u)-1.","cos(2u) when sin(u)=3/5|Use cos(2u)=1-2sin^2(u).|1-2*(9/25)=7/25.|No quadrant is needed for this result.","sin(2u) if sin(u)=3/5, cos(u)=4/5?","24/25."},{"Trigonometry","Oblique triangles","Law of sines: a/sin(A)=b/sin(B)=c/sin(C). Law of cosines: c^2=a^2+b^2-2ab*cos(C). SSA may have zero, one, or two solutions.","a=5, b=7, included C=60 degrees.|c^2=25+49-70*cos(60).|c^2=39.|c=sqrt(39), about 6.245.","a=3,b=4,C=90 degrees. Find c.","5."},{"Geometry","Lines and circles","Slope=(y2-y1)/(x2-x1). A vertical line has undefined slope. Circle: (x-h)^2+(y-k)^2=r^2.","x^2+y^2-4x+6y-12=0|Complete squares on x and y.|(x-2)^2+(y+3)^2=25.|Center (2,-3), radius 5.","Center of (x+1)^2+(y-4)^2=9?","(-1,4), radius 3."},{"Geometry","Conic sections","Ellipse: x^2/a^2+y^2/b^2=1. Hyperbola has a minus sign. Parabola: (x-h)^2=4p(y-k); focus (h,k+p).","x^2/25+y^2/9=1|Major axis horizontal, a=5,b=3.|c^2=a^2-b^2=16, so c=4.|Vertices (+/-5,0); foci (+/-4,0).","Focus of x^2=8y?","(0,2), since 4p=8."},{"Geometry","Vectors and polar","Vector magnitude sqrt(x^2+y^2). Dot product u1*v1+u2*v2. Polar: x=r*cos(t), y=r*sin(t); use quadrant when finding t.","Vector (3,4)|Magnitude sqrt(9+16)=5.|Unit vector (3/5,4/5).|Angle atan(4/3)=53.1301 degrees.","Dot product (1,2) dot (3,-1)?","1."},{"Sequences","Arithmetic sequences","a_n=a_1+(n-1)d. Sum S_n=n*(a_1+a_n)/2 for positive integer n.","a_1=4, d=3, n=10|a_10=4+9*3=31.|S_10=10*(4+31)/2.|Sum=175.","a_1=2,d=5. Find a_6.","27."},{"Sequences","Geometric sequences","a_n=a_1*r^(n-1). S_n=a_1*(1-r^n)/(1-r) for r!=1. Infinite sum a_1/(1-r) only if |r|<1.","a_1=8, r=1/2|Terms 8,4,2,1,...|Infinite sum=8/(1-1/2)=16.|Four-term sum=15.","Infinite sum 3+1+1/3+...?","9/2."},{"Sequences","Binomial and counting","nCr=n!/(r!(n-r)!). In (a+b)^n, term k+1 is nCk*a^(n-k)*b^k. Order matters for permutations, not combinations.","Coefficient of x^2 in (1+x)^5|Use k=2.|5C2=5*4/(2*1)=10.|Coefficient 10.","Choose 2 people from 6. How many groups?","6C2=15."},{"Systems","Two linear equations","Eliminate a variable or substitute. A zero determinant can mean no solution or infinitely many; compare equations.","x+y=5 and 2x-y=1|Add equations: 3x=6.|x=2.|Substitute: y=3.|Check both equations.","x+y=7 and x-y=1?","x=4, y=3."},{"Complex","Complex arithmetic","i^2=-1. Multiply normally, then replace i^2 by -1. Divide using the conjugate of the denominator.","(2+3i)*(1-4i)|Expand: 2-8i+3i-12i^2.|Replace i^2 by -1.|Answer: 14-5i.","(1+i)^2?","2i."},{"Calculator","Non-CAS workflow","Use Calculator for numeric evaluation and Graphs for visual checks. Non-CAS does not perform general symbolic algebra; show algebra yourself.","Check roots of x^2-5x+6.|Add a Graphs page and enter the function.|Use Analyze Graph > Zero around each crossing.|Expect 2 and 3.|Use Calculator to substitute and verify.","Why might sin(30) not equal 0.5?","The document may be in radians. Use degrees or enter pi/6 in radians."}}
-- Original numeric teaching engine; no CAS calls or trial dependencies.
function fmt(x)
 if x~=x or math.abs(x)==math.huge then error('Result is outside numeric range.') end
 if math.abs(x)<1e-12 then x=0 end
 return string.format('%.10g',x)
end
function need(ok,msg) if not ok then error(msg,0) end end
function integer(n) return n==math.floor(n) and n>=1 and n<=10000 end
TOOLS={
 {'Linear equation','a,b,c for a*x+b=c','2,3,11',function(v)
 local a,b,c=unpack(v); if a==0 then return {'0*x='..fmt(c-b),b==c and 'All real x solve this.' or 'No solution.'} end
 return {'Subtract b: a*x='..fmt(c-b),'Divide by a: x='..fmt((c-b)/a)} end,3},
 {'Quadratic roots','a,b,c for a*x^2+b*x+c=0','1,-5,6',function(v)
 local a,b,c=unpack(v); need(a~=0,'a must be nonzero. Use Linear equation.')
 local d=b*b-4*a*c; local h=-b/(2*a); local k=a*h*h+b*h+c
 local r={'D=b^2-4ac='..fmt(d),'Vertex h=-b/(2a)='..fmt(h),'Vertex k=f(h)='..fmt(k),'x=(-b +/- sqrt(D))/(2a)'}
 if d<0 then r[#r+1]='x='..fmt(h)..' +/- '..fmt(math.sqrt(-d)/math.abs(2*a))..' i'
 elseif d==0 then r[#r+1]='Repeated root: '..fmt(h)
 else local q=-0.5*(b+(b>=0 and 1 or -1)*math.sqrt(d)); r[#r+1]='Roots: '..fmt(q/a)..', '..fmt(c/q) end
 return r end,3},
 {'Line through points','x1,y1,x2,y2','1,2,3,8',function(v)
 local x,y,u,w=unpack(v); need(x~=u or y~=w,'Two distinct points are required.')
 if x==u then return {'Same x: vertical line.','Equation x='..fmt(x),'Slope is undefined.'} end
 local m=(w-y)/(u-x); return {'m=(y2-y1)/(x2-x1)='..fmt(m),'b=y1-m*x1='..fmt(y-m*x),'y=('..fmt(m)..')x+('..fmt(y-m*x)..')'} end,4},
 {'Two-equation system','a,b,c,d,e,f: ax+by=c; dx+ey=f','1,1,5,2,-1,1',function(v)
 local a,b,c,d,e,f=unpack(v); local det=a*e-b*d
 if det==0 then
 if (a==0 and b==0 and c~=0) or (d==0 and e==0 and f~=0) or a*f~=c*d or b*f~=c*e then return {'Determinant=0.','Inconsistent: no solution.'} end
 return {'Determinant=0.','Dependent: infinitely many solutions.'} end
 return {'D=ae-bd='..fmt(det),'x=(ce-bf)/D='..fmt((c*e-b*f)/det),'y=(af-cd)/D='..fmt((a*f-c*d)/det)} end,6},
 {'Exponential equation','a,b,c for a*b^x=c','3,2,21',function(v)
 local a,b,c=unpack(v); need(a~=0 and b>0 and b~=1 and c/a>0,'Need a!=0, b>0, b!=1, c/a>0.')
 return {'Isolate b^x=c/a='..fmt(c/a),'x=ln(c/a)/ln(b)','x='..fmt(math.log(c/a)/math.log(b))} end,3},
 {'Logarithm','base,value for log_base(value)','2,32',function(v)
 local b,x=unpack(v); need(b>0 and b~=1 and x>0,'Need base>0, base!=1, value>0.')
 return {'Change base: ln(value)/ln(base).','Answer='..fmt(math.log(x)/math.log(b))} end,2},
 {'Compound growth','P,r,t (r decimal per period)','100,0.05,3',function(v)
 local p,r,t=unpack(v); need(p>=0 and r> -1 and t>=0,'Need P>=0, r>-1, t>=0.')
 return {'Growth factor 1+r='..fmt(1+r),'A=P*(1+r)^t','A='..fmt(p*(1+r)^t),'Change A-P='..fmt(p*((1+r)^t-1))} end,3},
 {'Degree trig values','angle in degrees','30',function(v)
 local x=(v[1]%360)*math.pi/180; local s,c=math.sin(x),math.cos(x)
 return {'Radians=degrees*pi/180','sin='..fmt(s),'cos='..fmt(c),math.abs(c)<1e-12 and 'tan undefined at this angle.' or 'tan='..fmt(s/c)} end,1},
 {'Sine equation','s for sin(x)=s; degrees in [0,360)','0.5',function(v)
 local s=v[1]; need(math.abs(s)<=1,'Sine must be in [-1,1].')
 local a=math.asin(s)*180/math.pi; local x=a%360; local y=(180-a)%360
 return {'Principal asin(s)='..fmt(a)..' degrees','First angle='..fmt(x),x==y and 'Only one distinct angle.' or 'Second angle='..fmt(y),'General solutions: add 360*k.','k is any integer.'} end,1},
 {'Cosine law (SAS)','side a,side b,included C degrees','5,7,60',function(v)
 local a,b,c=unpack(v); need(a>0 and b>0 and c>0 and c<180,'Sides>0; included angle between 0 and 180.')
 local z=a*a+b*b-2*a*b*math.cos(c*math.pi/180)
 return {'c^2=a^2+b^2-2ab*cos(C)','c^2='..fmt(z),'c='..fmt(math.sqrt(z)),'Area=ab*sin(C)/2='..fmt(a*b*math.sin(c*math.pi/180)/2)} end,3},
 {'Arithmetic sequence','first term,difference,n','4,3,10',function(v)
 local a,d,n=unpack(v); need(integer(n),'n must be an integer from 1 to 10000.')
 local z=a+(n-1)*d; return {'a_n=a1+(n-1)*d='..fmt(z),'S_n=n*(a1+a_n)/2','S_n='..fmt(n*(a+z)/2)} end,3},
 {'Geometric sequence','first term,ratio,n','8,0.5,4',function(v)
 local a,r,n=unpack(v); need(integer(n),'n must be an integer from 1 to 10000.')
 local sum=0; local t=a; for i=1,n do sum=sum+t; if i<n then t=t*r end end
 return {'a_n=a1*r^(n-1)='..fmt(t),'Sum of first n terms='..fmt(sum),math.abs(r)<1 and 'Infinite sum=a1/(1-r)='..fmt(a/(1-r)) or 'Infinite geometric formula needs |r|<1.'} end,3},
 {'Combinations','n,r for n choose r','6,2',function(v)
 local n,r=unpack(v); need(n>=0 and n<=170 and n==math.floor(n) and r>=0 and r<=n and r==math.floor(r),'Integers: 0<=r<=n<=170.')
 local k=math.min(r,n-r); local z=1; for i=1,k do z=z*(n-k+i)/i end
 return {'nCr=n!/(r!*(n-r)!)','Cancel factorial factors before multiplying.','nCr='..fmt(z),'Order does not matter.'} end,2},
 {'Vector operations','ux,uy,vx,vy','3,4,1,0',function(v)
 local a,b,c,d=unpack(v); local u=math.sqrt(a*a+b*b); local w=math.sqrt(c*c+d*d); local dot=a*c+b*d
 local r={'|u|='..fmt(u)..'; |v|='..fmt(w),'u dot v='..fmt(dot)}
 if u>0 and w>0 then r[#r+1]='angle=acos(dot/(|u||v|))'; r[#r+1]=fmt(math.acos(math.max(-1,math.min(1,dot/u/w)))*180/math.pi)..' degrees' else r[#r+1]='Angle undefined for zero vector.' end return r end,4},
 {'Complex multiplication','a,b,c,d for (a+bi)*(c+di)','2,3,1,-4',function(v)
 local a,b,c,d=unpack(v); return {'Real part ac-bd='..fmt(a*c-b*d),'Imaginary part ad+bc='..fmt(a*d+b*c),'Answer ('..fmt(a*c-b*d)..') + ('..fmt(a*d+b*c)..')i'} end,4},
 {'Synthetic division','r,a,b,c,d: cubic / (x-r)','1,1,-6,11,-6',function(v)
 local r,a,b,c,d=unpack(v); local q=b+r*a; local z=c+r*q; local rem=d+r*z
 return {'Bring down a='..fmt(a),'Next b+r*a='..fmt(q),'Next c+r*previous='..fmt(z),'Remainder d+r*previous='..fmt(rem),'Quotient: ('..fmt(a)..')x^2+('..fmt(q)..')x+('..fmt(z)..')',rem==0 and 'x-r is a factor.' or 'x-r is not a factor.'} end,5}
}
function solve(index,input)
 local tool=TOOLS[index]; local values={}
 if input:match('^%s*,') or input:match(',%s*$') or input:match(',%s*,') then return {'Input error: empty field.'} end
 for s in input:gmatch('[^,]+') do
 local n=tonumber(s); if not n or n~=n or math.abs(n)>1e100 then return {'Input error: use finite decimal numbers.','Separate numbers with commas; no expressions.'} end
 values[#values+1]=n end
 if #values~=tool[5] then return {'Input error: expected '..tool[5]..' numbers.',tool[2]} end
 local ok,res=pcall(tool[4],values); if not ok then return {'Cannot solve:',tostring(res)} end
 return res
end
platform.apiLevel='2.0'
S={screen='home',selected=1,scroll=0,query='',input='',lesson=1,tool=1,answer=false,done={},score={}}
function redraw() platform.window:invalidate() end
function go(screen) S.screen=screen; S.selected=1; S.scroll=0; S.query=''; redraw() end
function items()
 local a={}
 if S.screen=='home' then return {{'Lessons & worked examples',1},{'Step-by-step calculators',2},{'Practice & progress',3},{'Help & calculator setup',4}} end
 local src=S.screen=='tools' and TOOLS or LESSONS
 for i,v in ipairs(src) do
 local name=S.screen=='tools' and v[1] or v[1]..': '..v[2]
 if name:lower():find(S.query:lower(),1,true) then a[#a+1]={name,i} end end
 return a
end
function ismenu() return S.screen=='home' or S.screen=='lessons' or S.screen=='tools' or S.screen=='practice' end
function lines()
 if S.screen=='lesson' then local l=LESSONS[S.lesson]; local a={l[3],'','WORKED EXAMPLE'}; for x in l[4]:gmatch('[^|]+') do a[#a+1]=x end; a[#a+1]=''; a[#a+1]='M: mark studied / unmark'; a[#a+1]='Status: '..(S.done[S.lesson] and 'studied' or 'not marked'); return a
 elseif S.screen=='quiz' then local l=LESSONS[S.lesson]; return {l[5],'',S.answer and ('Answer: '..l[6]) or 'Try it on paper. Enter reveals answer.',S.answer and 'Y: got it right   N: review again' or '',S.score[S.lesson] and ('Last result: '..S.score[S.lesson]) or ''}
 elseif S.screen=='result' then return S.result
 elseif S.screen=='input' then return {TOOLS[S.tool][2],'','Numbers separated by commas.','Decimals or scientific notation; no formulas.','All angle tools use DEGREES.','','Input: '..S.input,'','Enter: calculate   Del: erase','Tab: fill example'}
 else return {'PRECALCULUS STUDIO 1.0','Original lessons and numeric teaching tools.','36 lessons; 16 calculators; 36 practice prompts.','','Arrows: select / scroll. Enter: open.','Esc: back. In lists, type to filter.','Del: remove last typed character.','Lessons: M marks studied.','Practice: Enter reveals; Y/N self-assess.','Save this TNS document to retain progress.','','Tools use decimal numbers, not expressions.','Angle tools always use degrees, independent of document settings.','Answers are rounded to 10 significant digits.','This is a tutorial, not a general symbolic solver.','','Non-CAS check: add a Calculator or Graphs page to verify your work.','Graph a function, then use Analyze Graph to locate zeros or intersections.','Confirm document angle mode for trig checks.','','All features included; no activation or trial locks.'} end
end
function title()
 if S.screen=='lesson' or S.screen=='quiz' then return LESSONS[S.lesson][2] end
 if S.screen=='input' or S.screen=='result' then return TOOLS[S.tool][1] end
 return ({home='Precalculus Studio',lessons='Learn',tools='Calculate',practice='Practice',help='Help'})[S.screen] or 'Studio'
end
function wrap(gc,text,width)
 local out={}; local line=''
 for word in tostring(text):gmatch('%S+') do
 if gc:getStringWidth(line..(line=='' and '' or ' ')..word)>width and line~='' then out[#out+1]=line;line='' end
 while gc:getStringWidth(word)>width do local k=#word; while k>1 and gc:getStringWidth(word:sub(1,k))>width do k=k-1 end; if line~='' then out[#out+1]=line;line='' end;out[#out+1]=word:sub(1,k);word=word:sub(k+1) end
 line=line..(line=='' and '' or ' ')..word end
 out[#out+1]=line;return out
end
function on.paint(gc)
 local w,h=platform.window:width(),platform.window:height()
 gc:setColorRGB(248,250,252);gc:fillRect(0,0,w,h)
 gc:setColorRGB(23,48,77);gc:fillRect(0,0,w,29);gc:setFont('sansserif','b',11);gc:setColorRGB(255,255,255);gc:drawString(title(),8,5,'top')
 gc:setFont('sansserif','r',10)
 local cap=math.max(1,math.floor((h-66)/17));local y=34
 if ismenu() then
 local a=items();S.selected=math.max(1,math.min(S.selected,#a));local start=math.floor((S.selected-1)/cap)*cap+1
 for i=start,math.min(#a,start+cap-1) do
 if i==S.selected then gc:setColorRGB(214,232,244);gc:fillRect(3,y-1,w-6,17) end
 gc:setColorRGB(23,48,77); local label=a[i][1];while gc:getStringWidth(label)>w-18 do label=label:sub(1,-2) end;gc:drawString(label,8,y,'top');y=y+17 end
 gc:setColorRGB(70,85,100);gc:drawString(#a==0 and 'No matches. Del clears filter.' or (S.query~='' and ('Find: '..S.query) or (S.selected..' / '..#a..'  Enter: open')),8,h-29,'top')
 else
 local all={};for _,x in ipairs(lines()) do for _,z in ipairs(wrap(gc,x,w-16)) do all[#all+1]=z end end
 S.maxscroll=math.max(0,#all-cap);S.scroll=math.max(0,math.min(S.scroll,S.maxscroll))
 for i=S.scroll+1,math.min(#all,S.scroll+cap) do gc:setColorRGB(23,48,77);gc:drawString(all[i],8,y,'top');y=y+17 end
 gc:setColorRGB(70,85,100);gc:drawString('Lines '..(S.scroll+1)..'-'..math.min(#all,S.scroll+cap)..' / '..#all..'  Up/Down',8,h-29,'top')
 end
 gc:setFont('sansserif','r',9);gc:setColorRGB(70,85,100);gc:drawString('Esc: back   |   Learn - work - check',8,h-14,'top')
end
function on.arrowKey(key)
 local d=(key=='down' or key=='right') and 1 or -1
 if ismenu() then S.selected=math.max(1,math.min(#items(),S.selected+d)) else S.scroll=math.max(0,S.scroll+d) end;redraw()
end
function on.enterKey()
 if ismenu() then local a=items();local v=a[S.selected];if not v then return end
 if S.screen=='home' then go(({'lessons','tools','practice','help'})[v[2]])
 elseif S.screen=='tools' then S.tool=v[2];S.input='';go('input')
 else local practice=S.screen=='practice';S.lesson=v[2];S.answer=false;go(practice and 'quiz' or 'lesson') end
 elseif S.screen=='input' then S.result=solve(S.tool,S.input);go('result')
 elseif S.screen=='quiz' then S.answer=true;redraw() end
end
on.returnKey=on.enterKey
function on.escapeKey()
 local dest=({lesson='lessons',quiz='practice',input='tools',result='input'})[S.screen] or 'home';go(dest)
end
function on.charIn(c)
 if S.screen=='input' then if #S.input<160 then S.input=S.input..c;S.scroll=6 end
 elseif ismenu() and S.screen~='home' then if #S.query<35 then S.query=S.query..c;S.selected=1 end
 elseif S.screen=='lesson' and c:lower()=='m' then S.done[S.lesson]=not S.done[S.lesson]
 elseif S.screen=='quiz' and S.answer and (c:lower()=='y' or c:lower()=='n') then S.score[S.lesson]=c:lower()=='y' and 'correct' or 'review';end;redraw()
end
function on.backspaceKey() if S.screen=='input' then S.input=S.input:sub(1,-2) else S.query=S.query:sub(1,-2);S.selected=1 end;redraw() end
function on.tabKey() if S.screen=='input' then S.input=TOOLS[S.tool][3];redraw() end end
function on.save() return {done=S.done,score=S.score} end
function on.restore(t) if type(t)=='table' then S.done=type(t.done)=='table' and t.done or {};S.score=type(t.score)=='table' and t.score or {} end end
function on.resize() redraw() end
